{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.62,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["R12", "T4", "T5"],
      "pins": ["R12.2", "T4.3", "T5.1"],
      "nets": ["T5 gate node (T4.3/R12.1/T5.1)", "GND"],
      "obs": "In the ATO Valve driver the gate-bias resistor R12 (10k) is wired between the T5 (AO3400A) gate node and GND (a pull-DOWN), whereas the identical main-pump driver uses R5 (10k) as a pull-UP to +3V3. T4 (BT3904) is an NPN common-emitter sink (emitter to GND), so the T5 gate can only ever be pulled low; nothing raises it.",
      "exp": "With an NPN open-collector level shifter sinking a low-side N-MOS gate, the gate needs a pull-up to +3V3 (as R5 provides for T2) so that the MOSFET can turn on when the NPN is off. The spec's intended ATO valve switch (T3/T4/R10) is expected to actually energize the solenoid.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "ATO Valve: 'R12 10k' drawn from the T5 gate node down to a ground symbol, while Main Pump shows 'R5 10k' drawn from +3V3 down to the T2 gate node (sheet 1 bottom / sheet 3)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T3 — AON6407 ... ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch ... gate driven through R10 (100 Ω), pre-driven via T4 (BT3904)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The ATO solenoid valve gate is permanently held at ground, so T5 never conducts and the valve can never open regardless of the ATO_VALVE GPIO. Automatic Top-Off, a core feature, would fail to operate.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["PR1", "H1", "U3", "U4"],
      "pins": ["H1.5", "PR1.TR", "U3.8", "U4.8"],
      "nets": ["EZO_PDIS", "I2C_SDA", "I2C_SCL"],
      "obs": "The 'Water Height Sensor' block wires the TF-Luna LiDAR PR1 to header H1, connecting PR1 VCC/SCL/SDA to +5V/I2C_SCL/I2C_SDA and PR1 TR to H1 pin 5, which carries the EZO_PDIS net. Thus the isolator power-disable control net is merged with the sensor header / LiDAR trigger.",
      "exp": "Spec §4.3/§6 state PR1's pins are typed 'free' and it is not connected to any net (on_board: no); spec §4.2 states EZO_PDIS ties only U3.8, U4.8 and IO6. The LiDAR should not load the I2C bus nor share the EZO_PDIS control net.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Water Height Sensor: PR1 LiDAR pins VCC/SCL/SDA/GND/TR/RX to H1; H1 pin1=+5V, pin3=I2C_SDA, pin4=I2C_SCL, pin5=EZO_PDIS (sheet 1)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "the r2 netlist shows PR1 ... all four pins (VCC, SDA, SCL, GND) typed free — i.e., it is not connected to any net"}
      ],
      "impact": "An unpopulated-by-firmware device is added to the I2C bus and the EZO_PDIS disable line is bridged to the sensor header; toggling IO6 to power-cycle the isolators also pulses the LiDAR trigger, and the extra bus load can disturb I2C.",
      "confidence": 0.45
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["T3", "T5"],
      "pins": ["T3.1", "T5.1"],
      "nets": ["+24V input", "ATO_VALVE"],
      "obs": "The AON6407 (T3) is used as the 24 V input reverse-polarity switch (with R7/D3), and the ATO solenoid is switched by the small SOT-23 AO3400A (T5).",
      "exp": "Spec §2 assigns the AON6407 (T3) to the ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch; a 24 V solenoid with only a 30 V-rated, low-current SOT-23 MOSFET is marginal.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "POWER TRAIN: 'T3 AON6407' on the +24V input with R7 33k/D3 12V; ATO Valve: 'T5 AO3400A' as the solenoid switch (sheet 1)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "T3 — AON6407 (8-DFN N-MOSFET) | ATO solenoid-valve low-side switch"}
      ],
      "impact": "The valve MOSFET is a smaller part than intended (30 V SOT-23) with limited margin against solenoid inrush and flyback spikes; combined with the R12 gate fault the valve path is unreliable.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing contains at least one clear functional deviation: in the ATO valve driver the gate-bias resistor R12 is tied to GND (pull-down) instead of +3V3 like the main pump's R5, so with the NPN sink T4 the solenoid MOSFET T5 can never turn on and top-off fails. Lower-confidence deviations also appear: the TF-Luna LiDAR PR1 is wired onto the I2C bus and its trigger bridged to the EZO_PDIS control net (spec says PR1 is unwired), and the AON6407 intended for the valve appears on the input instead."
}

